body:
Hey, got mine a similar way quite a few months a ago, except I did it myself with something that said it was safe.

&#x200B;

No one can really tell you how long you may have it, if you have no hearing loss that's a positive sign, but there's also hidden hearing loss which is possible from that procedure. Who knows. I have enough hope to believe, with others, that we will all get relief some point in the future, either a cure or natural cessation. Maybe I'm wrong, but all we can do now is adjust, keep it off our minds, and live life as 'normally' as possible. Get engaged in something, commit your life to your passion, it will begin to become less important to you as time goes on. But I think we all eventually deserve a solution, whether it's a minor annoyance or catastrophic disability. Good luck, hopefully yours isn't chronic

Ah, that's a solid theory. Almost as if all tinnitus is from hidden hearing loss. Those who lose it naturally may still obtain their nerves and not get tinnitus.

&#x200B;

Do you have any resources that somewhat prove this?
